organization: CSIRO Division of Radiophysics/Australia Telescope National Facility
keywords: Karma visualisation toolkit
newsgroups: comp.windows.x,alt.security.pgp,comp.security.misc,comp.graphics.visualization,comp.sys.sun.apps,comp.unix.aix,comp.unix.osf.misc,comp.unix.solaris,comp.unix.ultrix,sci.image.processing


Version 1.4 of the Karma library is now available for ftp. The Karma
library is a general purpose programmers toolkit (see below).

	Karma is available for anonymous ftp from:  ftp.atnf.csiro.au
  under the  pub/software/karma  directory. Both the source code and binary
  distributions are kept here. The source code is available free of charge.
  There is also a WWW page for the library:
    http://www.atnf.csiro.au/karma/
  In addition, the ATNF visualisation software, which uses the Karma
  library, also has a WWW page:
    http://www.atnf.csiro.au/Software/Analysis/visualisation/

  Binary distributions for:
	SunSparc, SunOS 4.1.3
	SunSparc, Solaris 2.5
	i386, Linux 1.2.8 and 2.0.x (ELF)
	mips1, Ultrix V4.3 (Rev. 44)
	alpha, OSF/1 V3.2 (Rev. 148)
	hp9000, HP-UX A.09.01
	mips4, IRIX 6.0.1
	rs6000, AIX 3.2
  are available in addition to the source distribution.

Notable changes since 1.3:

1)  Partial refresh support added to the graphics library. This allows
"damage repair" algorithms which provide a fast way to "undraw"
objects in complex scenes.

2)  Attributes for PostScriptPage objects are now defined,
particularly the <KWIN_ATT_LINEWIDTH> attribute.

3)  Support for DirectColour colourmaps has been added. The user may
now control the primary colour components in a DirectColour visual.

4)  Miriad Image masks are now supported.

5)  Non-integral zooming is now supported. It is now possible to zoom
in an image by a non-integral factor.

6)  Decreasing co-ordinate systems are now supported by the data
format as well as the graphics library.

7)  Panning supported added to the <viewimg> package. This has been
used in the kview display tool to implement a fast magnifying glass
window.

8)  The <wcs> package has been created, supporting proper astronomical
sky projections.

9)  Optimisations for reading and writing non-byte data types on
byte-swapped (little endian) machines has been added (4x to 5x
faster).

10)  GIPSY (Groningen Image Processing SYstem) format files are now
supported by the <foreign> package.

11)  Volume rendering tool <xray> now contains a 3-dimensional
cursor. See the ATNF visualisation WWW page for information.

12)  Library documentation (reference manual) has been completely
reformatted. The HTML version contains complete cross-referencing
active links, and is visually much more appealing.

13)  New user interface for zoom control (just left-click, drag and
release to zoom).

14)  New slider widget created. Looks like a real slider.

15)  New display tool to interactively show Position-Velocity images
(astronomy specific).

16)  Various extra features, bugfixes and optimisations.

See the release notes for more details. Below are README extracts:

===============================================================================
				Karma

		    A powerful programmers toolkit


	Karma is a toolkit for interprocess communications,
  authentication, encryption, graphics display, user interface and
  manipulating the Karma network data structure. It contains KarmaLib
  (the structured libraries and API) and a large number of modules
  (applications) to perform many standard tasks.

  When files and directories are referred to, they are given relative to the
  root Karma directory (environment variable KARMABASE if defined). This is
  usually  /usr/local/karma
  Please see the file  INSTALL  for instructions on how to install Karma.

  The update policy for Karma is in the file  doc/update-policy

  The  doc/lib  directory contains documentation for the Karma libraries.

  The  doc/modules  directory contains documentation for the various Karma
  modules. This directory may be a little sparse...

  The  doc/howto  directory contains information on how to make good use of
  some of the more interesting packages in KarmaLib.

  The  doc/widgets  directory contains information on the Karma Widgets
  library. This directory may be a little sparse...

	Please mail any bug reports to:  karma-bugs@atnf.csiro.au
  No warranty, express or implied should be inferred by this mailing address.

	If you want to be added to the mailing list (to find out what's changed
