Found what I think are 2 bugs in the standard Digital UNIX
cc compiler this week.

Not sure of the OS version, but I think it is 3.2 patch
level 148. 


The first one is that >> on a full unsigned  long of
1 bits fails to do anything. This is a standard trick
I use to to find the largest +ve 2 complement number.

The second is that the compiler does not recognise hex
chars. It was leathfull because I had it in a test
for characters below space which cause a lookup on a
table to core dump.

	if ( khar < 'x20)
		tbl[khar].xxxx

I'll be interested to hear if anyone agrees with my
findings.

